{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783596-the-displaced-fan-made-seeming","id":783596,"title":"The Displaced, fan made Seeming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T12:58:04-08:00","id":783596,"title":"The Displaced, fan made Seeming","content":"After reading on the 2nd Edition changes to the Seemings, Kiths, and the relationship between the two, not to mention hearing of the addition of at least two more Seemings, I started thinking of a new Seeming to fit with the old style fairy tale vibe I was getting.<br /> <br /> Technically, the Displaced have two 'sub-seemings', one focused on time, the other on space, both function the same, just a different emphasis on either side of space-time.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cNot all those who wander are lost.\u201d - J.R.R. Tolkien</i><br /> <br /> The Displaced doesn't seem to fit right in, or maybe they're just a bit out of place or out of sync with everyone else. Perhaps they follow foreign customs or speak in an archaic tongue. They are the ones looking for a home, a place to fit in, a time that makes sense to them. But they're all wanderers, and when the whims of fate hits, they'll wander once again.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>You will know a Displaced by the way their accent, actions, clothes, maybe even their stance. You can feel that they're not suppose to be there, or that it's not their place. But they try, they really do. But their attempts at fitting in makes them, at best, look like bumbling fools, or, at worst, look like an insulting satire.<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>They were once a pillar of the community, some person of renown or someone who helped everyone in their time. But things change. Perhaps they wanted to see the world, or break out of a boring routine. To see the sights and go to times and places exotic. The desire to leave grows within them, bit by bit. Until they run to the Keeper for just one adventure, or were tricked by a seeming benign offer.<br /> <br /> <b>Escape:</b> They ran away from reality and into a fantasy. In their Durance, they witnessed wonders and horrors, excited and suffered by their Keeper. But, sooner or later, they lose interest and look back to their homes in yearning. Some wander Arcadia, knowing the destination but not the path, others lose their sense of time, not knowing if hours or centuries had passed. In losing their sense of direction or time as they focus on home, they found a way to escape.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Creation:</b> Displaced are wanderers but highly perceptive, if at least knowing the difference between their surroundings to their old home makes them as such. Ironically, they make excellent guides, scouts, and sentries. They have an easier understanding of actual social relations for they see things in the eyes of an outsider.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Clarity of Difference. Things change, even if the same events happen again or happen in a separate place, they'll be different that what happened before. They notice this and learn more of their new surroundings or perhaps try to introduce new ideas to the new place or revive ideas from an old time.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Yearning for Home. They'll try to fit in, to once again be a part of their new community. But their difference would only make them stand out. Any time they try to fit in, only to be excluded from the group, is a Clarity Break.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts: </b>They say his head is in the clouds. Thinking about spaceships and rayguns, he acts as if he lived centuries from now. But, from time to time, one can notice the shine of a chrome raygun in his pocket.<br /> She stands in front of the old style microphone. Swaying left and right as she sings a jazz cover of some pop song. But one can't help but look at her, listen to her voice, and imagine themselves backwards in time to some lost black and white film.<br /> Some look at the man as if he's some bumbling tourist or some exotic traveler in his yacht. But to him, he looks at the island in the distance, his old home, so close yet so far away. Obstacles are placed before him but he'll find a way home.<br /> <br /> The ideas that inspired the Displaced are Rip Van Wrinkle and other fairy tales where the character returns home from fairyland centuries later, for the time Displaced, and the Odyssey, for the space Displaced. In my opinion, the Displaced are probably the closest in human appearance but with the sense of difference that makes them hard to fit in,<br /> <br /> <b>Kith examples:</b><br /> <br /> Antiquarian - He appears to be an actual medieval scribe, or perhaps act like one.<br /> <br /> Artist - She appears to be an artist of light, using strange tools to create holographic masterpieces.<br /> <br /> Manikin - He appears to be imitating an old fashion idea of what a robot looks like.<br /> <br /> Whisperwisp - She appears to be a ninja, with silent steps and sharp hearing.<br /> <br /> Skogsra - He appears to be a throwback to the Stone Age, or perhaps a dirty image of a barbarian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6163-yama951","name":"Yama951","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T13:06:50-08:00","id":783603,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea, but I don't know if it really encapsulates what Seemings are about. Seemings (to my understanding) are supposed to embody or reflect how the character regains Agency and escapes Arcadia. This Seeming just doesn't feel empowering or a source of agency to me. They just wandered away. It doesn't have the philosophical &quot;punch&quot; of the Elementals' &quot;letting go of their sense of self&quot; or the Beasts' abandonment of their humanity. It just feels like it misses the mark on what a Seeming is supposed to be, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T13:15:42-08:00","id":783610,"title":"","content":"It's more of trying to 'get a sense of belonging once again', like trying to live out your life after finding out everything changed during a trip. The main problem is that Changeling is basically the game of trying to get back home/make a new home again. So I really don't know what to put for the Displaced as it's theme other than being more lost than the Lost and being an outsider trying to fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6163-yama951","name":"Yama951","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T13:16:00-08:00","id":783611,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's no reclaimation here. There's no embrace of a principle that makes you larger than a world.<br /> <br /> It's also trying to tap into a fairy tale archetype that's common experience more than role, so there's that oo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T13:23:13-08:00","id":783617,"title":"","content":"I think you can rework this into a homebrewed Kith. Or two, if you want to keep the Time-Displaced and Space-Displaced different.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Displaced are those changelings who were taken by whimsical True Fae that immediately forgot about them, and left them to wander a beautifully mad world, rather than sculpted into a specific purpose. Perhaps the Displaced are those that escaped their Keeper's attention and, rather than escaping into the Hedge, simply wandered Arcadia until something happened to them that made them want to regain their agency and come back home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T01:19:32-08:00","id":783995,"title":"","content":"I most disagree with you on this not being Seeming - Displaced have Agency - <b>they want to return to <i>their</i> time-place</b>. You are lost now, as this place ( present Earth ) is not <i>your</i> times, but you will try to make this - or find way to it. You run from True Fae when you understood they live in ever Maybe, not here and now, not <b>yours</b> place nad time. You split from Arcadia realm without time and place to Earth to look for your way back - and you <i>will</i> find it. Or you will be lost forever.<br /> <br /> I even think that Displaced would most dedicated in understanding of workings of Wyrd. They would the one to travel Hedge to find finally portal to <i>their </i>time or place. If not this it Agency, I do not know what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T01:54:58-08:00","id":784011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783596-the-displaced-fan-made-seeming?p=783995#post783995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I most disagree with you on this not being Seeming - Displaced have Agency - <b>they want to return to <i>their</i> time-place</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>All seemings want to return home, and simply wanting to go home is not having agency. How do these guys actually get out? They went &quot;I'm bored&quot; and that's enough?.... To be honest, it sounds like the keeper let them escape and that they should just be seemingless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T04:33:51-08:00","id":784053,"title":"","content":"I think the real problem is that they do or don't have Agency, and more that they never really lost their Agency. Part of their story was that they wanted to wander, and when they decided they were done, they tried to go home. Both steps of the journey were theirs to make. Honestly, it seems to me to be a case of a Seemingless changeling, or an interesting couple of Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T10:01:30-08:00","id":784228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783596-the-displaced-fan-made-seeming?p=783995#post783995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I most disagree with you on this not being Seeming - Displaced have Agency - <b>they want to return to <i>their</i> time-place</b>.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> If not this it Agency, I do not know what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanting something is not agency. <i>Doing</i> something is agency. It's about facing and overcoming a conflict, taking control back, empowering yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T12:15:14-08:00","id":787553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/783596-the-displaced-fan-made-seeming?p=783995#post783995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If not this it Agency, I do not know what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wanting something is not agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanting something is indeed not agency. The two points above aside here is my take:<br /> <br /> From what I can tell about Seemings, they involve deep cognitive self-transformation that removes part of their psyche, ability to trust for darklings, sense of self for elementals, inhibition towards violent for ogres, the separation of their identity from their craft for wizen, inhibition towards breaking social norms for beasts, indifference towards the suffering of others for the fairest. All these losses are important coping mechanisms for getting along in society and produce severely unbalanced people when they are absent. Changeling is a game of Madness, beautiful or grotesque as it may be and these core game mechanics ensures that it is.<br /> <br /> If you are making a seeming that could be counted as &quot;well-adjusted&quot; you've missed the mark of what Seemings are, and their purpose for enforcing game themes. Seeming are the spiritual/psychological/metaphysical scars needed to escape Arcadia , acquired like a fox chewing off its foot to escape a trap, and their purpose is to enforce the themes of the struggle out of madness, chasing after broken coping mechanisms, and relapse caused emotionally devastating psychological triggers. I mean look at the blessing and curse of all the existing seeming, that is exactly what they represent and seeming only mechanical purpose seems to enforce these themes in a variety of ways that are interesting for the story.<br /> <br /> Every Seeming needs a well written blessing and curse to fulfill these goals. Also it should be easy to identify what the changeling cut out of their psyche to escape. Your curse is really well written and I think exactly what you were shooting for. Well done. Your blessing and what part of their being they cut away from themselves is a little muddled. Part of the problem is that the existing seemings cover the cutting out very broad pieces of the Lost's psyche, and many ideas that could fit this potential seeming are mere small subsections of existing seemings. Also the themes of wanting a home and not being able to find one should be worked right into the mechanics of the seeming. Here is a possible revision:<br /> <br /> The Displaced doesn't seem to fit right in, or maybe they're just a bit out of place or out of sync with everyone else. They are the ones looking for a home, a place to fit in, a time that makes sense to them. But they're all wanderers, and when the whims of fate hits, they'll wander once again.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> Clarity of New Beginnings. When a Departed abandons his long term associations, belongings and home to make a new beginning unfettered to their past they regain a point of Clarity.<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> Can't find Home. They'll try to fit in, to once again be a part of their new community. But their difference would only make them stand out. Any time they try to fit in, only to be excluded from the group, or deal with abandoned associations or return to a previous home, it is a Clarity Break.<br /> <br /> I will not tell you what I intended for this to remove from the changeling's psyche, because I hope it is clear enough I don't have to. I will proudly say it enforces the themes you had for the Departed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}